{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01J8wbN6NffbEbNF22iVg5df","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to generate detailed imagined experiment data for all \"planned\" experiments in the experiment_plan, based on the \"median\" tier definition they provided. Let me identify all planned experiments:\n\n1. plan_006 - Gradient conflict analysis on v7 (3 epoch checkpoints)\n2. plan_007 - Attention heatmap visualization\n3. plan_009 - Llama-3.1-8B Phase 1 GAR degradation diagnosis\n4. plan_010 - Llama-3.1-8B ThreadGate v7 training\n\n\n5. plan_011 - Llama-3.1-8B LoRA-only training\n6. plan_012 - Llama-3.1-8B 3-way eval\n7. plan_013 - Llama-3.1-8B gradient conflict analysis\n8. plan_014 - Downstream task sanity check\n9. plan_015 - Statistical significance analysis (bootstrap CI)\n10. plan_016 - Exposure-bias mitigation test\n\nFor each, I need to produce detailed predictions consistent with the median tier: Llama-3 reproduces the failure trend but with weaker magnitude, mitigation results remain ambiguous, and claims need to be narrowed.\n\nNow I'm laying out the specific metric ranges I expect to see across these experiments—relative performance drops, training-inference gaps, gradient similarities, and mitigation effectiveness bounds that all align with this median scenario.\n\nFor the Qwen gradient conflict analysis, I'm pulling from existing data in the documentation showing how cosine similarity and magnitude ratios shift across checkpoints, and I need to formalize those observations into a structured experiment plan with full YAML specifications.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":19954,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":19954},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagn